# No test-document content in code

Product code must work for **any** `.docx` template. Do not bake in labels, values, company names, case numbers, or tick glyphs from the file currently open in preview / QA fixtures.

## Forbidden in production code (`src/`, `public/app.js`, server prompts)

- Field names or values copied from a sample/test doc
- Glyph allowlists (`✓` `√` `✔` …) to decide bool vs text
- Stem/keyword lists from a sample letter (`โทร`, `แฟกซ์`, field captions, company names)
- Manual cache-bust tokens like `?v=web83` — use content hash (`publicAssetUrl`)
- Defaulting bool `trueText` to a fixed mark — use the cell sample or the model instead

```ts
// ❌ BAD
if (/^(fieldA|fieldB)$/.test(header)) …
if (/^[✓√✔☑]$/u.test(cell)) return "bool";
trueText = "√";
```

## Prefer

- Structure from **this** file: column headers, tabs, prototype row, numbered-list stems found in XML
- Shape classes: `isSymbolOnlyCell` / `\p{P}` `\p{S}`, digits → auto
- Prompts that describe patterns, not one template’s words

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
const name = resolveVarName(columnHeader, lang);
if (isSymbolOnlyCell(cellText)) return "bool"; // trueText = cellText
```

## OK

- App chrome UI copy (Thai)
- Smoke/fixture files under `scripts/` with invented sample text
- Format-only prompt examples (`Label\\tValue`) with fake placeholders
- OOXML / `{{…}}` syntax

## When unsure

If it only works for the preview doc, do not ship it.
